:""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/888-thatblueguy","name":"ThatBlueGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar888_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T18:07:05-08:00","id":31365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=31010#post31010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm jealous. I want to see who liked some of my random posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T18:16:29-08:00","id":38529,"title":"","content":"Going to throw in some personal canon here and there while I'm waiting for the wiki to come back.<br /> <br /> <b>Ribbons that Bind - Eastern Goddess of Slavery</b><br /> Ribbons that Bind appears as a woman of remarkable beauty unmarred by her dishevelled appearance, long blonde hair conceals much of her face and she is clad only in rags that scarcely cover her occasionally exposing great welts and bruises upon her fair skin. She is invariably chained and bound by a creature that resembles a great two-headed minotaur that is known only as The Minion of Suffering there have been at least two instances when a would-be hero has attempted so save the goddess from her own bodyguard and lover.<br /> It\u2019s the subject of much debate if Ribbons that Bind truly enjoys her treatment or if she has taught herself to endure what her charges must and that The Minion of Suffering is a means to that end.<br /> <br /> The greatest threat to Ribbons that Bind comes from her brother Ribbons of Sorrow who desires the position of Eastern God of Slavery for himself. In battle (usually against her brother\u2019s assassins) the two employ a special fighting chain that allows the Minion of Suffering to use his mistress as an improvised flail. The power of the chain allows vitality to flow back and forth between the two of them making them a surprisingly formidable team considering that one of them is literally throwing the other around like a rag doll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 12-28-2013, 09:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T08:32:21-08:00","id":38745,"title":"","content":"Okay, that is fragging awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T19:15:43-08:00","id":39033,"title":"","content":"<b>Godparents in Creation:</b><br /> During the Time of Glory it was a tradition in many human communities for a couple to pray to a particular god or deva shortly after a child\u2019s birth and make what sacrifices they could in the hope that the spirit took notice and agreed to protect the child.<br /> Often these prayers were ignored or the spirit in question agreed but considered the child a very low priority but tales of a god being impressed by the prayer and sacrifice of mortals and taken up this duty have passed into legend.<br /> <br /> The conventional role of godparents fell out of favour in the First Age and was later considered a heresy of the Immaculate Faith which instead taught children to emulate the Elemental Dragons who would reward them by allowing them to eventually reincarnate as Dragon-Blooded. The concept of godparents became somewhat demonised by tales of overzealous spirits that would remove any and all obstacles to its charge\u2019s desires eliminating siblings and potential love rivals along with enemies.<br /> <br /> The resurgence of this custom in the Age of Sorrows was brought about mostly by the Fair Folk. A surprising number of Raksha have found the comparison to a god flattering and offered oaths to guarantee the infant\u2019s safety (with certain loopholes of course, just to keep things interesting). Demons also tend to be receptive to such requests, the notion that mortals would request that denizens of Malfeas protect their children is often met with delight in the demon city and seen as a sign that Creation is lost without the Primordials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:01:18-08:00","id":40383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=39033#post39033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Godparents in Creation:</b><br /> During the Time of Glory it was a tradition in many human communities for a couple to pray to a particular god or deva shortly after a child\u2019s birth and make what sacrifices they could in the hope that the spirit took notice and agreed to protect the child.<br /> Often these prayers were ignored or the spirit in question agreed but considered the child a very low priority but tales of a god being impressed by the prayer and sacrifice of mortals and taken up this duty have passed into legend.<br /> <br /> The conventional role of godparents fell out of favour in the First Age and was later considered a heresy of the Immaculate Faith which instead taught children to emulate the Elemental Dragons who would reward them by allowing them to eventually reincarnate as Dragon-Blooded. The concept of godparents became somewhat demonised by tales of overzealous spirits that would remove any and all obstacles to its charge\u2019s desires eliminating siblings and potential love rivals along with enemies.<br /> <br /> The resurgence of this custom in the Age of Sorrows was brought about mostly by the Fair Folk. A surprising number of Raksha have found the comparison to a god flattering and offered oaths to guarantee the infant\u2019s safety (with certain loopholes of course, just to keep things interesting). Demons also tend to be receptive to such requests, the notion that mortals would request that denizens of Malfeas protect their children is often met with delight in the demon city and seen as a sign that Creation is lost without the Primordials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Nice! Using this! Was this something talked about in the old forums? It seems familiar.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:03:09-08:00","id":40386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hailey McAuliffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=31365#post31365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm jealous. I want to see who liked some of my random posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There I liked your post, and now you know. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T00:11:24-08:00","id":40392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=40383#post40383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Very Nice! Using this! Was this something talked about in the old forums? It seems familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've talked about it before.<br /> It goes back to the first Exalted game I ran, the PCs developed this bizarre love of Octavian and part of the epilogue was the Wood Aspect asking the Quarter Prince to keep a watchful eye upon his newborn daughter, Octavia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:04:20-07:00","id":94487,"title":"","content":"I'm going to post some Hekatonkhire because I'm still waiting on the wiki.<br /> <br /> <b>The Sleeper in the Lake</b><br /> Though the Sleeper in the Lake is not one for words theories of its origin speculate that it was once the ghost of a boy who drowned when the one responsible for his safety became distracted in the arms of a lover. The boy became a Spectre and somehow gained access to a Neverborn\u2019s tomb where his nightmares briefly became one with that of the Neverborn and remade him as a tall broad shouldered man with a simple bone coloured mask and wielding a Soulsteel machete named \u201cinnocence\u201d for it was all that remained of the little boy who drowned in the lake.<br /> <br /> Nobody knows if this story is true or not, but when he\u2019s not controlled directly by Deathlords or Abyssals The Sleeper of the Lake has an uncanny way of homing in upon young lovers.<br /> <br /> <b>The Unity of Bones</b><br /> It is believed that the Unity of Bones was created when one of the dying Primordials knew what it was to be truly alone for the first time in its existence. The voices of its multitude of souls silenced as life slipped away from it.<br /> The Unity of Bones exists for a simple purpose, to bring the dead, the dying and the living together in the most expedient way possible. It doesn\u2019t speak but those able to communicate with it through other means learn that it considers itself on a holy mission to avenge anyone that ever died alone.<br /> A Void Circle Necromancer can summon the Unity of Bones using two corpses of individuals that loved each other in life and arranging their bones in a manner that makes them one in death and only through this act can the Hekatonkhire be called into Creation. <br /> Initially little more powerful than a zombie the Unity of Bones can become devastatingly powerful if given access to a necropolis or a bloody battlefield as it incorporates the bodies into its mass and rapidly grows to terrifying size.<br /> <br /> <b>The Creature of Haggard\u2019s Keep</b><br /> Nobody even has a good guess where this Hekatonkhire came from or how it came to lose one of its eyes. Despite being several hundred feet tall it is surprisingly light upon its feet and wherever it travels so too does a thick bank of grey clouds that allow no light to pass through save for the blinding white-blue beam of its one remaining eye that sweeps the area like a search light.<br /> Those who are caught by its gaze feel the essence ripped from them as it is used to feed the creature and while its rampages may be dangerous they are nothing compared to what The Creature of Haggard\u2019s Keep would be capable of if engorged on essence, it is a small mercy that its missing eye impedes it in that capacity. If the two were to be reunited then the Underworld could be in great danger.<br /> <br /> <b>Shiver</b><br /> Unlike most Hekatonkhire Shiver was created as part of an experiment by the Daybreak The Fairest and Fallen by imbuing the quicksilver blood of the Neverborn with raw soul stuff endowing it with a rudimentary sentience and some shape shifting ability.<br /> While Shiver rarely takes the same form for very long it is capable of forming knife like protrusions and forming basic shapes to facilitate its mistress\u2019 desires. Possibly the most interesting thing about Shiver is how it seems to become affectionate towards the Daybreak, coiling around her like a serpent when inert or repairing from damage. It is from this tendency that it gained its name.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fortress of Bone</b><br /> A wedge shaped mass of bone a couple of miles long with a green hue to it, the Fortress of Bone is believed to have been an important soul of a Primordial prior to the war as it occasionally recalls that it used to be something far greater than its current form. The Fortress is an extremely powerful Hekatonkhire capable of flight and creating simulacra from its black vicious blood but limited by a need for a master in order to be capable of exerting its full power.<br /> To become the Master of the Fortress of Bone might seem like a tantalising proposition but it\u2019s also a trap. Those who become the Master of the Fortress find it intruding upon their thoughts and only the strong willed can compel themselves to take a course of action without it, in time they are simply unable to leave. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:28:51-07:00","id":94501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=94487#post94487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Awesome Hekatonkhires</div> </div> </div> </div>These are super awesome, even more so due to the dearth of homebrew Hekatonkhires. I'm definitely going to have to use these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:40:16-07:00","id":94507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=94487#post94487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Sleeper in the Lake</b><br /> Though the Sleeper in the Lake is not one for words theories of its origin speculate that it was once the ghost of a boy who drowned when the one responsible for his safety became distracted in the arms of a lover. The boy became a Spectre and somehow gained access to a Neverborn\u2019s tomb where his nightmares briefly became one with that of the Neverborn and remade him as a tall broad shouldered man with a simple bone coloured mask and wielding a Soulsteel machete named \u201cinnocence\u201d for it was all that remained of the little boy who drowned in the lake.<br /> <br /> Nobody knows if this story is true or not, but when he\u2019s not controlled directly by Deathlords or Abyssals The Sleeper of the Lake has an uncanny way of homing in upon young lovers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pair this up with some Dragon Blooded summer camp councilors, and I see the makings of a great Halloween mini campaign!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1522-turkeygiant","name":"turkeygiant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1522_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"999"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T09:38:48-07:00","id":116992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Noodle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=94501#post94501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are super awesome, even more so due to the dearth of homebrew Hekatonkhires. I'm definitely going to have to use these.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've speculated based on what we know of the Liminal Exalted thus far that they're going to have 'cousins' who came back wrong that are considered a type of Hekatonkhire rather than Exalts. Pandorans to their Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:19:53-07:00","id":117015,"title":"","content":"This is why we can't have nice things! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:32:09-07:00","id":117025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=94487#post94487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to post some Hekatonkhire because I'm still waiting on the wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me see if I can get them all:<br /> <br /> <b>The Sleeper in the Lake</b> : Jason<br /> <b>The Unity of Bones</b> : I think some monster in Eberron does this?<br /> <b>The Creature of Haggard\u2019s Keep</b> : Cloverfield<br /> <b>Shiver</b> : Terminator<br /> <b>The Fortress of Bone</b> : The Dark Gundam?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T10:50:54-07:00","id":117036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=117015#post117015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why we can't have nice things! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I tried to pull the whole Caine tangent out the topic but soon discovered that was a bit like trying to pull a thread from a sweater. We're better off with a new thread to talk about Evocations anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=117025#post117025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me see if I can get them all:<br /> <br /> <b>The Sleeper in the Lake</b> : Jason<br /> <b>The Unity of Bones</b> : I think some monster in Eberron does this?<br /> <b>The Creature of Haggard\u2019s Keep</b> : Cloverfield<br /> <b>Shiver</b> : Terminator<br /> <b>The Fortress of Bone</b> : The Dark Gundam?</div> </div> </div> </div>3/5 I'm not sure where The Unity of Bones came from but I've got very little experience with Eberron beyond a short-lived Pathfinder game. The Fortress of Bone is based on the Citadel of Bone from Super Robot Monkey Team Hyperforce Go! Which despite the silly name and obvious Sentai inspiration has a main villain who is unnervingly similar to a Deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 04-21-2014, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:39:57-07:00","id":117064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=117036#post117036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried to pull the whole Caine tangent out the topic but soon discovered that was a bit like trying to pull a thread from a sweater. We're better off with a new thread to talk about Evocations anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, I'm not saying <i>you're</i> the reason we can't have nice things; you made the right call.<br /> <br /> But it had to be said, and this seemed the most suitable place to say it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T20:25:47-07:00","id":117356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=94487#post94487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike most Hekatonkhire Shiver was created as part of an experiment by the Daybreak The Fairest and Fallen by imbuing the quicksilver blood of the Neverborn with raw soul stuff endowing it with a rudimentary sentience and some shape shifting ability.<br /> While Shiver rarely takes the same form for very long it is capable of forming knife like protrusions and forming basic shapes to facilitate its mistress\u2019 desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It doesn't work that way, but it can form solid metal shapes.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Like what?<i>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Knives and stabbing weapons</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> I enjoy using those lines at least once in every game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T09:02:36-07:00","id":182937,"title":"","content":"I'm currently really unsure about the Emissary of Nexus as an NPC, I'm not sure if this is 2e isms that have created this problem or if it's something I have with the core concept.<br /> <br /> My issue is that most places in Creation that have avoided being ground to dust under the boot heel of a supernatural powerhouse like the Realm or a Deathlord have used guile and cunning, to generally play to the strengths of their inhabitants. The Three combined their powers to create a story that threatened to reveal the Princess Magniifcent's secret weakness and the Perfect of Paragon escaped Realm domination by exploiting the fact that they didn't know how his Sceptre worked.<br /> <br /> In contrast to this the city of Nexus has resisted thanks to a mysterious figure who'll kill you if you obstruct trade. Someone who routed a Realm Legion by murdering its chain of command and beat up a Third Circle Demon... it's rather jarring. I think my biggest issue is that they've gradually destroyed the possibility that the Emissary is a charlatan which would be the most characterful option for Nexus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-28-2014, 12:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:02:26-07:00","id":182995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=182937#post182937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In contrast to this the city of Nexus has resisted thanks to a mysterious figure who'll kill you if you obstruct trade. Someone who routed a Realm Legion by murdering its chain of command and beat up a Third Circle Demon... it's rather jarring. I think my biggest issue is that they've gradually destroyed the possibility that the Emissary is a charlatan which would be the most characterful option for Nexus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine if all those things were actually done by other people that found it useful to attribute the result of their actions to the Emissary for various reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/292-zironic","name":"Zironic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar292_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"654"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:21:49-07:00","id":183021,"title":"","content":"Honestly, in 2E where Thorns was close enough to be part of a trade group &amp; therefore close enough to be a threat, charlatan was very iffy. 3E sounds like it has enough room to move Thorns away (and a lot of the body count could have been lies, or copycats, or powerful people covering their tracks by blaming someone else). I think the only plausible charlatan in an Exalted world has always been 'figurehead &amp; assassin bait surrounded by group of powerful folks who do the real supernatural work'<br /> <br /> Considering that 3E is reflavoring/remechanic-ing a bunch of creature types, the Emissary might be a good place to show examples.<br /> 1. A set of very powerful artifacts/big evocation tree. Hm. If you die &amp; reattune your artifacts after becoming a ghost, do you keep the evocations?<br /> 2. One of the new style elementals. Maybe they'll have powers that can pull this off.<br /> 2. Guild shenanigans. A bunch of mostly-anonymous folks, uncertain power level, but who have access to a Guild's worth network of Fair Folk items, Artifacts, etc.<br /> 3, Eldest member/founder of one of the new Exalt types.<br /> 4. Humanoid behemoth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:45:50-07:00","id":183055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zironic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=182995#post182995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine if all those things were actually done by other people that found it useful to attribute the result of their actions to the Emissary for various reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware of the golden rule (the Realm Legion thing has room for ambiguity but RoGD2 outright states that the Emissary of Nexus defeated Jacint) but I feel I've lost sight of much of what he really added to the city in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T10:57:36-07:00","id":183063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=183055#post183055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm aware of the golden rule (the Realm Legion thing has room for ambiguity but RoGD2 outright states that the Emissary of Nexus defeated Jacint) but I feel I've lost sight of much of what he really added to the city in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div> The novel that depicts that happening basically says &quot;Emissary floats up to Jacint, lifts his mask &amp; stares at him, Jacint recognises the Emissary, freaks out and goes gone to Malfeas&quot; It's been a while since I read it (dawn of the Sun maybe? Pretty sure it was the first book in the trilogy) but that's a fairly accurate recount of what happened while Dace &amp; co were fighting Zsofika and horde in the streets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/649-nightwinder","name":"Nightwinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:01:00-07:00","id":183064,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there some sort of face-beam involved too?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T11:41:12-07:00","id":183109,"title":"","content":"If you go the &quot;Emissary is a charlatan&quot; route you pretty much have to assume that the Emissary has enough hustle to occasionally get people with superpowers to play its part or contract out miracles that it can take credit for. I don't like it if this ends up being a commonplace occurrence, but it's essential that it happen sometimes, because the emissary swans around with no personal guard and eventually <i>somebody</i> is going to be bold enough to jump it with a posse and try to take its mask off, especially in a game with PCs in it. It's a delicate matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T13:57:22-07:00","id":183205,"title":"","content":"The Emissary is actually three puppies standing on top of each other with a robe, and a mask of levitation. Jacint fled not out of fear or defeat but because the realization he'd been bluffed that long by small dogs; the thing with the Realm legions was just a really big misunderstanding about how fetch works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T15:07:48-07:00","id":183271,"title":"","content":"I don't really mind the Emissary-as-real-entity so much just because it's the Lady of Pain to Nexus' Sigil.<br /> <br /> Something's gotta keep all those angels and demons from stabbing each other in the streets all the time, and trying to conquer the place all the time, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T10:29:53-07:00","id":200214,"title":"","content":"<b>Plot seed: The Prophet of Doom</b><br /> The PCs meet a dirty and dishevelled looking man who has travelled a long way to see them. It\u2019s almost impossible to get much of a conversation out of this man without learning his most strongly held belief; he genuinely believes the end of the world is rapidly approaching.<br /> <br /> What immediately differentiates him from the typical madman is that he seems to know the player characters far better than a stranger has any right to and his insights about how the end will come about are uncomfortably specific almost as though he lived through it himself, but that\u2019s impossible\u2026 isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Unfortunately his experiences have rendered him rather insane and the more the PCs attempt to interrogate him on his version of events the more disjointed and incoherent his version of events will become.<br /> <br /> Can they be trusted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:07:28-07:00","id":200261,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly imagining him in one of our games before 3e hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:37:28-07:00","id":200284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=200261#post200261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suddenly imagining him in one of our games before 3e hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlikely, he's the wrong tone for Roaring20s and Great Forks has already had a cryptic warning of a bad future. Unless someone else uses him he's just going to gather dust on my ideas shelf, so I posted him here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T13:14:36-07:00","id":259163,"title":"","content":"I did a bad thing...<br /> <br /> <b>Light of the Black Lantern</b><br /> Cost: 25+m<br /> Target: One Corpse<br /> Gaining access to a corpse that possessed great virtue in life, the Necromancer summons a flame that radiates darkness rather than light and constructs a lantern in order to house it as part of a ritual that takes a minimum of three days.<br /> At the end of this time the Necromancer must speak the corpse\u2019s name, their home in life or place of birth and the command to rise.<br /> <br /> The newly forged Revenant begins with traits equivalent to a zombie save for its enlightened essence with a pool of 10 motes. And a limit track. The Necromancer may increase ability ratings at 1m per dot, raise attributes at 2m per dot, improved essence rating at 8m per dot, willpower at 4m per dot and finally charms at 3m per dot. Any given trait is limited by what the Revenant knew in life and any charms are dark mirrors of any magical capacities they once possessed (determined by the Necromancer\u2019s player and the Storyteller).<br /> <br /> The Revenant possesses the Motivation to destroy whatever legacy it created in life and will be relentless in this purpose regardless of the Necromancer\u2019s wishes.<br /> <br /> The Lantern has two purposes; first of all it prevents the Revenant from attacking the Necromancer (or anyone else who might be holding the lantern) and secondly it may be used to override the Revenant\u2019s imperative to destroy with more immediate commands.<br /> These orders last for about a day and cause the Revenant to gain a point of limit. At 10 points of limit the Lantern is powerless to order the Revenant or protect the Necromancer from their creation\u2019s wrath. Fortunately, a point of limit is lost whenever the Revenant achieves significant progress towards wiping out its legacy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T13:55:11-07:00","id":259199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=259163#post259163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a bad thing...<br /> <br /> <b>Light of the Black Lantern</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any idea what would have happened if you had written this, like, a month ago?<br /> <br /> I would have harassed Flare to let me have it relentlessly.<br /> <br /> And right now the Red Pupil would be hunted down by their own Revenant brother! Such irony. So perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:29:46-07:00","id":259241,"title":"","content":"I feel it has a certain personal touch that a Bone Lion lacks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T14:45:42-07:00","id":259248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=259199#post259199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have any idea what would have happened if you had written this, like, a month ago?<br /> <br /> I would have harassed Flare to let me have it relentlessly.<br /> <br /> And right now the Red Pupil would be hunted down by their own Revenant brother! Such irony. So perfect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wonder how well that would have turned out for you...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T10:31:56-07:00","id":260740,"title":"","content":"This thread reminds me how much I miss the wiki. Such a great collection of homebrew. Such a useful tool for looking up unexplained, unreferenced hearthstones in NPC textblocks. One day the wiki's shard will return to us in a new host!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:29:35-07:00","id":268330,"title":"","content":"So today I start writing a custom charm for the Shogunate Dragon-Blooded game I'm in.<br /> <br /> Essentially my character in that is an Earth Aspect engineer who rides a self-made Dragonwheel (a Low First Age equivalent of a Road Lion combined with a TRON Light Cycle) and I've been working on a Martial Art for her to give her a more unique fighting style. So I look at the charm I've just written and realise I've written an indisputable 3rd edition charm for a 2nd edition game with no clear idea how to backport it!<br /> <br /> It's slightly worrying that Third Edition seems to be overwriting Second Edition in my brain already...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:35:27-07:00","id":268336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=268330#post268330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's slightly worrying that Third Edition seems to be overwriting Second Edition in my brain already...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's really not. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T06:32:39-07:00","id":272180,"title":"","content":"At least the Chase rules from Shards are a thing in 2nd edition.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T14:17:11-07:00","id":272471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=268336#post268336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's really not.</div> </div> </div> </div>In fairness, it <i>can</i> be worrying, if you're a playtester worried about inadvertently giving away EX3 spoilers without realizing it.<br /> <br /> But yeah, long-term? I <i>definitely</i> see it as a plus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T08:34:04-08:00","id":375274,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Bronze_Marcus_Aurelius_Louvre_Br45.jpg/396px-Bronze_Marcus_Aurelius_Louvre_Br45.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> This inspired me recently, It's a fragment of a bronze portrait of Emperor Marcus Aurelius that's on display in the Louvre.<br /> I saw it in the course of my daily rumaging and had a mental image of someone finding a statue of their previous incarnation and overlaying it on their face and looking in the mirror... possibly while laughing madly. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T08:45:13-08:00","id":375284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XG63OtsKC7k\" data-code=\"XG63OtsKC7k\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/XG63OtsKC7k/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T12:49:02-08:00","id":378291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=375274#post375274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This inspired me recently, It's a fragment of a bronze portrait of Emperor Marcus Aurelius that's on display in the Louvre.<br /> I saw it in the course of my daily rumaging and had a mental image of someone finding a statue of their previous incarnation and overlaying it on their face and looking in the mirror... possibly while laughing madly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Laughing madly is good...though it strikes me as so solemn and sad a cast that I think weeping would be more appropriate...that may just be my mental state, of course. <br /> It would also be interesting to have them incorporate it into a helm as a faceguard or such...lots of possibilities in that fragment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T16:47:01-08:00","id":383798,"title":"","content":"I think it can work with a variety of tones, I was just aluding to the scene with the Joker in the 1989 Batman movie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:34:33-07:00","id":636101,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest fear as a moderator is that one day I'm going to accidently ban someone and delete all their posts because they jokingly started a thread with a spammy title and a seemingly unrelated link because my brain goes into batch processing mode when I encounter a wall of spam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T14:02:49-07:00","id":636254,"title":"","content":"{Is never going to start a thread again}","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T03:41:11-07:00","id":636865,"title":"","content":"Alright, no more new threads guys. Shut it down.<br /> <br /> Close the forums from orbit. It's the only way to be sure [that no one gets accidentally banned].","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Don't feel bad. People tell the developers they get Exalted wrong all the time. -hippokrene","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4729-childofthesun1","name":"Childofthesun1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4729_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"853"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T03:15:50-07:00","id":637817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=636101#post636101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest fear as a moderator is that one day I'm going to accidently ban someone and delete all their posts because they jokingly started a thread with a spammy title and a seemingly unrelated link because my brain goes into batch processing mode when I encounter a wall of spam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As someone who cleans out the dregs of the internet on a daily basis, I empathize with this. Course, my oversight is next-to-non-existent, soooo....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T09:48:42-07:00","id":649067,"title":"","content":"So my Resonance conclusions.<br /> <br /> Essentially that in most games I've seen with Renegade Abyssals have the character(s) in question through a shitstorm of consequences from walking away from a Deathlord while dealing with the stigma of being Anathema and a Creature of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Resonance has a tendency to feel redundant and impersonal while that is going on. So my thoughts are that it should lurk in the background and cause the lion\u2019s share of its problems for Abyssals who\u2019ve found safety and acceptance building primarily during the uneventful days until it makes them eventful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:04:52-07:00","id":649244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=649067#post649067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my Resonance conclusions.<br /> <br /> Essentially that in most games I've seen with Renegade Abyssals have the character(s) in question through a shitstorm of consequences from walking away from a Deathlord while dealing with the stigma of being Anathema and a Creature of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Resonance has a tendency to feel redundant and impersonal while that is going on. So my thoughts are that it should lurk in the background and cause the lion\u2019s share of its problems for Abyssals who\u2019ve found safety and acceptance building primarily during the uneventful days until it makes them eventful.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes sense, although it's worth noting that the various personality/behavior mechanics have usually been massively overdetermined if they exist at all. Like, once you determine eligibility for Limit or Clarity or &amp;c, the mechanics put you on a strict path with not a lot of room for judgment calls of any sort. At the other end of the scale you have 1E Sidereals, who didn't have any kind of behavior/personality mechanic at all, just some narrative guidelines for their flavor of the Great Curse.<br /> <br /> What you're describing sounds... actually, it sounds a lot like breaking an Eclipse oath, come to think of it! The Eclipse oaths split the difference there; they have a mechanical underpinning and mechanical guidelines, but they also put a lot of power in the hands of the GM via narrative control for when breaking the oath is gonna rear up and nail you. It isn't a perfect analogy, Resonance isn't so much about &quot;punish you for going renegade&quot; as it is &quot;even if you go renegade, you're still destroying the world, whatcha gonna do about <i>that</i>, my fine friend?&quot;, but it sounds like what you're saying is that if Resonance is going to be like that, it needs more granular controls than what it has now, where it is kind of massively impersonal and that isn't fit for purpose.<br /> <br /> I should try and track down my old Promethean books actually, because this is a really great idea for Resonance and it also sounds a bit like what the Prometheans had going (where if they stopped and tried to be normal for too long the universe started rejecting them) and I'm curious if there's mechanical goodness to be gleaned from there as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:26:09-07:00","id":649264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=649244#post649244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the other end of the scale you have 1E Sidereals, who didn't have any kind of behavior/personality mechanic at all, just some narrative guidelines for their flavor of the Great Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was my experience that the 1E presentation of the Sidereal Great Curse translated to &quot;Sidereals are always controlled by the Great Curse&quot; for a lot of people, most prominently for that one scenario in Exalted: the Autochthonians where they removed themselves from play for the duration of the crisis by behaving like the Central Bureaucracy from Futurama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=649244#post649244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should try and track down my old Promethean books actually, because this is a really great idea for Resonance and it also sounds a bit like what the Prometheans had going (where if they stopped and tried to be normal for too long the universe started rejecting them) and I'm curious if there's mechanical goodness to be gleaned from there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> That might be on the right lines.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T13:51:00-07:00","id":649281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">a bit like what the Prometheans had going (where if they stopped and tried to be normal for too long the universe started rejecting them)</div> </div> </div> </div> Prometheans had two things of that type, which you're conflating a little bit here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Disquiet was the effect they had on people and communities, in which extended proximity gradually gave a sense that there was something off about the Created which would culminate in strong impressions and occasional glimpses of their true nature and appearance, combined with a kind of infection from the concentrated intensity of their Pyros, which would create harmful associations with the character (often a desire to drive them away, but for one group an obsessive need to possess them); Wasteland was an effect the Promethean had on the environment, in which staying in one place for two long would cause one's Pyros to start corrupting and warping the landscape to reflect the elemental association of the character (so Frankensteins would cause increased electrical discharges culminating in extreme lightning storms). <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if there's mechanical goodness to be gleaned from there as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's got a fairly straightforward &quot;roll resistance against Power Stat&quot; thing (Prometheans have a number of advantages and disadvantages assocaited with their Power Stat along with a way to decrease it, so they've got a balancing act there).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T22:04:53-07:00","id":649768,"title":"","content":"I think if the main reason Resonance should be different from Disquiet is that it should primarily be a beacon for Creatures of Death and causing ripple effects that help aspects of the Abyssal\u2019s old life to catch up to her. Any aspect of turning people against you should be secondary to them being exposed to the Abyssal's dark and troubled past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:13:10-07:00","id":650278,"title":"","content":"Disquiet should probably not be applied to Abyssals. At least not in the First edition of Disquiet. Wasteland though could be awesome for Abyssals: stay too long in one place and the ground loses nourishment, slowly killing plants, slowly driving people away from their home, leaving only you and a ghost-town in a barren, deserted wasteland of your own creation.<br /> <br /> No matter where you go, you'll always kill creation a little more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T10:35:23-07:00","id":650295,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind all I was saying is &quot;hey, the Promethean 'the universe hates you' mechanics and themes might have some useful or valuable things to tell us about hypothetical rebuilds of the Abyssals 'hey, you're here to kill the world' mechanics and themes.&quot;<br /> <br /> I wouldn't suggest simply cut-and-pasting either disquiet or wasteland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T05:02:24-07:00","id":657658,"title":"","content":"I may not be the best person to contribute, here, because I tend to loath punishment mechanics, period, But...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=649067#post649067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my Resonance conclusions.<br /> <br /> Essentially that in most games I've seen with Renegade Abyssals have the character(s) in question through a shitstorm of consequences from walking away from a Deathlord while dealing with the stigma of being Anathema and a Creature of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Resonance has a tendency to feel redundant and impersonal while that is going on. So my thoughts are that it should lurk in the background and cause the lion\u2019s share of its problems for Abyssals who\u2019ve found safety and acceptance building primarily during the uneventful days until it makes them eventful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Resonance was always the most brutal and inflexible of the Curse (and its variants).<br /> <br /> Personally, I would just toss the concept of Resonance out entirely, and build a Limit track that leverages collateral damage and unintended consequences in their power set. Their anima banners kill things, and they tend to not grow back. Their disease Charms are a bit too effective when they are used at times. I would overlay that on your idea of an abiding Curse, so it's not just a power-up. The Abyssal is extra-murdery not necessarily when it's convenient, but when it's most effective.<br /> <br /> I'd also try to build in large paths that allow Renegades to mostly play well with others and not be completely screwed, because that was the somewhat-fatal flaw of Abyssals in 2E. People loved, them, but they didn't get played nearly as much because Resonance was a harsh mistress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T07:07:05-07:00","id":685683,"title":"","content":"Wasn't sure where else to post this...<br /> <br /> The Eye and Seven Despairs in my games took a curious evolution from comedy to nightmare fuel.<br /> <br /> The first time I used him started out as a parody of the MoEP: Abyssals version with the Prioress of Bloody Sands persona obviously him in a crude disguise.<br /> <br /> Somehow this worked really well for him, because despite having read the book my PCs didn\u2019t treat Star of Dirt and Doubt with the least bit of suspicion because after the ridiculousness of the Prioress they expected nothing from him.<br /> <br /> Now the players were Renegade Abyssals who\u2019d teamed up with Chorus at Midnight and helped her get rid of Scar of Uproar who weirdly showed up again despite having been confirmed killed (the Midnight Caste actually ate him it's hard to get more dead than this). So they go exploring Cold House and discover a room with a woman who has recently undergone reconstructive surgery to look like Chorus at Midnight at the behest of her master. They also found Chorus\u2019 Monstance which was crafted in her likeness begging the question of if she even looked like herself or if he\u2019d remade her into the likeness of his old circlemate.<br /> <br /> They immediately stopped treating Eye and Seven Despairs like a joke...<br /> <br /> Future portrayals of Eye and Seven Despairs have really built on that moment of horror while discarding the silly canonical aspects and play him up as the mad scientist Deathlord.<br /> <br /> In the current portrayal he\u2019s known to obsess over cadavers where he spends weeks or months analysing a dead body to learn as much as he can of the circumstances of death and make deductions on who they were in life. Invariably cloning them to observe them at different stages of development and when the subject fascinated him greatly allowing those clones to go out into the world and replace the original because they bring something to the world that was \u201clacking\u201d.<br /> <br /> As a patron he\u2019s disinterested virtually everything, so his Abyssals are allowed to run the show while he occupies the lower levels of Cold House like a monster living in the basement who occasionally emerges to bestow a gift that will aid in one of his Deathknights goals showing that sometimes he does pay attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:27:56-07:00","id":685804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=685683#post685683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't sure where else to post this...<br /> <br /> The Eye and Seven Despairs in my games took a curious evolution from comedy to nightmare fuel.<br /> As a patron he\u2019s disinterested virtually everything, so his Abyssals are allowed to run the show while he occupies the lower levels of Cold House like a monster living in the basement who occasionally emerges to bestow a gift that will aid in one of his Deathknights goals showing that sometimes he does pay attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reminds me of Paranoia, which would lead me to suggest... Sometimes he emerges and bestows a gift. Other times it is &quot;I have a new experimental plague to test / kill-only-ghost soulbreaker orb to test / go get me a corpse killed by (something bizarre, rare, and deadly) / take this clone and make it a powerful governor in An-Teng&quot;<br /> <br /> So, generally friendly as long as you feed E7D's mania, and as long as it doesn't need an Abyssal test subject. Good way to get the PCs to visit all corners of creation.<br /> <br /> Personally, if I could figure out a way I'd use bits from the &quot;scientists&quot; in Bleach. Mayuri and Szayelaporro are just evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:39:42-07:00","id":685808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=685683#post685683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a patron he\u2019s disinterested virtually everything, so his Abyssals are allowed to run the show while he occupies the lower levels of Cold House like a monster living in the basement who occasionally emerges to bestow a gift that will aid in one of his Deathknights goals showing that sometimes he does pay attention.</div> </div> </div> </div> I imagine that's more fun for the players too, as they can do the things they want, just knowing he's around so they better not break theme and start trying to help everybody. So you still have the core of &quot;He's your evil boss&quot; and he can occasionally hand out plot if you want, but they still feel like the main characters of the story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-02T08:46:39-07:00","id":685824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=657658#post657658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may not be the best person to contribute, here, because I tend to loath punishment mechanics, period, But...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, Resonance was always the most brutal and inflexible of the Curse (and its variants).<br /> <br /> Personally, I would just toss the concept of Resonance out entirely, and build a Limit track that leverages collateral damage and unintended consequences in their power set. Their anima banners kill things, and they tend to not grow back. Their disease Charms are a bit too effective when they are used at times. I would overlay that on your idea of an abiding Curse, so it's not just a power-up. The Abyssal is extra-murdery not necessarily when it's convenient, but when it's most effective.<br /> <br /> I'd also try to build in large paths that allow Renegades to mostly play well with others and not be completely screwed, because that was the somewhat-fatal flaw of Abyssals in 2E. People loved, them, but they didn't get played nearly as much because Resonance was a harsh mistress.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did any of you play with the Dark Fate from Shards? That's what we use for the (I really, really hope) rogue Abyssal in our power. It seems to work far better than the previous game with a rogue Abyssal in, who got tons of resonance from being friendly with us.<br /> On the other hand, it is just a slightly modified Limit rules, and perhaps could be more interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> People talking about Disquiet and Wasteland makes me think of the original Resonance rules though: one effect was to have people turn against you, another was for you to look more undead, another was to blight the land, blacken mirrors, spread chill winds, etc.<br /> I think there was some good ideas there, it's just the actual mechanic of how you got it and lost it worked badly. The intimacy-twisting one was one I disliked too, because it slowly turned you into a character who just hated everything, which ought to be a player choice/depend on things that happen in the game.<br /> <br /> I do also think that Resonance might be better refluffed as a natural effect of an Abyssal's blighted essence, rather than a punishment handed out by the Neverborn, but that's a matter of taste I suppose. It'd give the writers a bit more flexibility in what could and couldn't work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-25T00:45:29-07:00","id":725338,"title":"","content":"There's something extremely cathartic about watching all those Second Edition threads get washed away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:22:55-08:00","id":826410,"title":"","content":"Something I want to do something with but have no idea where or how I'll use it.<br /> <br /> The Delzhan nomads aren't the original inhabitants of Chiaroscuro and there's no indications in CoTD: South that these people were wiped out. So I like the idea that they're still around in the present day as a marginalised group that's shared many cultural traditions with the Delzhan but retains its own distinct cultural identity.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure what it will be or how they're different yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T17:45:27-08:00","id":826419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826410#post826410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I want to do something with but have no idea where or how I'll use it.<br /> <br /> The Delzhan nomads aren't the original inhabitants of Chiaroscuro and there's no indications in CoTD: South that these people were wiped out. So I like the idea that they're still around in the present day as a marginalised group that's shared many cultural traditions with the Delzhan but retains its own distinct cultural identity.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure what it will be or how they're different yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense, and will hopefully appear if we put out a book covering Chiaroscuro in detail.<br /> <br /> (Ethnic divisions of this sort were a big feature in an extensive Goldenseal write-up for my home game.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T20:48:08-08:00","id":826514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826419#post826419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense, and will hopefully appear if we put out a book covering Chiaroscuro in detail.<br /> <br /> (Ethnic divisions of this sort were a big feature in an extensive Goldenseal write-up for my home game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an excellent possible blog post!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T21:18:19-08:00","id":826531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826410#post826410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I want to do something with but have no idea where or how I'll use it.<br /> <br /> The Delzhan nomads aren't the original inhabitants of Chiaroscuro and there's no indications in CoTD: South that these people were wiped out. So I like the idea that they're still around in the present day as a marginalised group that's shared many cultural traditions with the Delzhan but retains its own distinct cultural identity.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure what it will be or how they're different yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they may not have been wiped out, but after a few centuries it's likely most have been culturally assimilated, as tends to happen in the realworld (see Eggpt, or the Anatolian peoples). But, it is also possible some still exist in small enclaves (see Sorbs, Assurians, and Frisians). I look forward to your thoughts on what they were like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T02:27:37-08:00","id":826659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826410#post826410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I want to do something with but have no idea where or how I'll use it.<br /> <br /> The Delzhan nomads aren't the original inhabitants of Chiaroscuro and there's no indications in CoTD: South that these people were wiped out. So I like the idea that they're still around in the present day as a marginalised group that's shared many cultural traditions with the Delzhan but retains its own distinct cultural identity.<br /> <br /> I'm just not sure what it will be or how they're different yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, Chiaroscuro is like Nexus in the sense that it's that kind of city that is so cosmopolitan that one can't really designate anybody who lives there as the &quot;original inhabitants&quot;, which is a characteristic it retains even into the period in which the Delzhan happen to be the dominant ethnic group. I mean, the idea is supposed to be that the Delzhan took over the city at the time when the numerous warring factions within it, several of whom had entered in the aftermath of the Contagion, had exhausted the First Age arsenals fighting it out amongst themselves, so even if I was inclined to picture there as being a core group of &quot;Chairoscurans&quot;, they would have been people who would have been mixed up with innumerable newcomers from various areas for centuries before the Delzhan even arrived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T04:14:39-08:00","id":826695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826419#post826419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes sense, and will hopefully appear if we put out a book covering Chiaroscuro in detail.<br /> <br /> (Ethnic divisions of this sort were a big feature in an extensive Goldenseal write-up for my home game.)</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> So. How do you take your bribes for sharing this?<br /> <br /> Or just inspiration for Goldenseal?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:10:40-08:00","id":826711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=826659#post826659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, Chiaroscuro is like Nexus in the sense that it's that kind of city that is so cosmopolitan that one can't really designate anybody who lives there as the &quot;original inhabitants&quot;, which is a characteristic it retains even into the period in which the Delzhan happen to be the dominant ethnic group.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've found it tended to translate into 'all Delzhan all the time' ingame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean, the idea is supposed to be that the Delzhan took over the city at the time when the numerous warring factions within it, several of whom had entered in the aftermath of the Contagion, had exhausted the First Age arsenals fighting it out amongst themselves, so even if I was inclined to picture there as being a core group of &quot;Chairoscurans&quot;, they would have been people who would have been mixed up with innumerable newcomers from various areas for centuries before the Delzhan even arrived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely. The &quot;True Chiaroscuran&quot; is as real as the true Scotsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-09-2016, 08:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T05:52:16-08:00","id":826742,"title":"","content":"I keep seeing the i and a getting mixed up in &quot;Chiaroscuro&quot; and its derivatives, and I keep imagining a city of giant glass chair-shaped buildings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:12:26-07:00","id":862922,"title":"","content":"The response to the spoiler thread <b>wouldn't fucking lock</b> so I tossed it into quarantine.<br /> I know people don't like it when stuff disappears. I'm sorry, I do the best that I can with the tools I have and sometimes they feel like a rubber chicken and a paperclip.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:13:56-07:00","id":862923,"title":"","content":"Why are you apologizing for shitty forum software? The explanation was enough, IMO. Appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:20:45-07:00","id":862926,"title":"","content":"I don't mean to be critical, but the thought of things I've expressed being beyond my reach causes me a lot of anxiety, so I need to at least vent a little bit to relieve that some before I try sleeping:<br /> <br /> Would it not be possible to end a thread with the equivalent to a forum wide thread ban? To just state &quot;don't post here anymore&quot;, with mild to moderate punishment for flagrant violations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:22:33-07:00","id":862927,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> It happens, you did what you could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:33:04-07:00","id":862934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=862923#post862923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you apologizing for shitty forum software? The explanation was enough, IMO. Appreciate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm using sorry to indicate that I empathise with people who don't like their posts disappearing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=862926#post862926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it not be possible to end a thread with the equivalent to a forum wide thread ban? To just state &quot;don't post here anymore&quot;, with mild to moderate punishment for flagrant violations?</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is to lock and review the discussion leading up to infactions in the interest of fairness and I've just spent most of the last three hours watching the daring rescue of a mother and son from a nest of Kaleyi and a disease spirit in league with the Pale Mistress.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:37:25-07:00","id":862935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=862922#post862922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know people don't like it when stuff disappears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because you usually don't tell us that they disappeared, or even why. This time you did, so we're cool (we were always cool).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 04-09-2016, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T18:45:06-07:00","id":862937,"title":"","content":"didnt wirk everythjings still too loud going to try watchuingshit","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:04:07-07:00","id":862947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=862922#post862922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The response to the spoiler thread <b>wouldn't fucking lock</b> so I tossed it into quarantine.<br /> I know people don't like it when stuff disappears. I'm sorry, I do the best that I can with the tools I have and sometimes they feel like a rubber chicken and a paperclip.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sucks.<br /> <br /> However, the thread was almost a mirror of the one that spawned it, only with more vitriol. It's not much of a loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:26:48-07:00","id":862961,"title":"","content":"Mhm, there were some good points at the very beginning before the filibuster descended in force, but all things considered it's probably better that nobody knows who got the last word in that thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:30:53-07:00","id":862963,"title":"","content":"Say, unrelated but curious, how does one refer to another poster like I've been seeing lately, the one where it's a link to their profile and that poster gets a notification about the mention?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:35:54-07:00","id":862964,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a>, you use an @.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:39:21-07:00","id":862966,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> you gotta do it with the &quot;@&quot; symbol.<br /> <br /> Edit: dammit, didn't refresh the page for 4 minutes and this is what happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T19:45:58-07:00","id":862970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=862963#post862963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, unrelated but curious, how does one refer to another poster like I've been seeing lately, the one where it's a link to their profile and that poster gets a notification about the mention?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The forum member may not get the notification if they turn the &quot;Mentions you (@username) in a post&quot; option off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:56:37-07:00","id":896720,"title":"","content":"A little work in progress.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Mist, Chosen of Revolutions</b></b><br /> You've probably all heard the tales of how the farmer Mist ventured into the Wyld and was assimilated into the narrative of the Eternal Revolutionary. He gained power, won his victory but paid a great personal cost as Mist the man became lost in Mist the legend.<br /> <br /> In this version of events, he was prevented from entering the Wyld by Tahn Jo, the God of Righteous Revolts and Uprisings who had been a farmer himself in his mortal life. The two of them swore a pact under Heaven to liberate Kahla and be the heroes that this fallen age needed them to be, apparently the Unconquered Sun heard them.<br /> <br /> Excellencies:<br /> A Chosen of Revolutions is a master of improvisation strengthened by their personal notions of right and wrong. Mist has a dice cap of (Attribute) but when acting in accordance with an Intimacy he may convert up to (Intimacy Rating) dice into successes at a cost of 1m per dice.<br /> <br /> Offensive Charms:<br /> Denounce the Tyrant (10m, 1wp; Simple; Instant; Decisive-only) see the write-up of Mist, the Eternal Revolutionary for details.<br /> <br /> Covert Charms:<br /> Symbol of Outrage (4m, Simple, Instant, Mute) Mist chooses an oppressed group that he's spent one or more scenes interacting with and appropriates a symbol of their oppression as one of revolution. The symbol can only communicate a simple idea like anger, shame or the desire for freedom in the target group but is meaningless to anyone else.<br /> <br /> Craft Charms:<br /> Arming the Masses (Permanent) Mist's best work is not only innovative but also simple to follow and building upon existing skills. Those who witness him complete a basic projects may emulate it without penalty provided they posess a conceptually relevant craft and adequate tools.<br /> <br /> The Agent of Chaos<br /> At the back of Mist's mind lives a persona that craves anarchy rather than justice; it sometimes appears to him in various guises but has no physical form of its own.<br /> The Agent of Chaos has its own charms and traits, it\u2019s quite eager to help Mist in its various guises but each scene in which he accepts its aid he gains a point of limit and its visitations become more frequent cumulating in his limit breaks which he experiences as bouts of missing time. Was this something that Tahn Jo passed onto him or did he turn to a questionable source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-23-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:07:34-07:00","id":896731,"title":"","content":"*Slightest* of tweaks- I'd suggest that the Chosen of Revolutions should only be able to draw on Principles, not on intimacies in general.<br /> <br /> Stories about Revolutions are full of examples of people putting their ideals before their personal relationships (often to the detriment of both)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:15:17-07:00","id":896734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=896731#post896731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Slightest* of tweaks- I'd suggest that the Chosen of Revolutions should only be able to draw on Principles, not on intimacies in general.<br /> <br /> Stories about Revolutions are full of examples of people putting their ideals before their personal relationships (often to the detriment of both)</div> </div> </div> </div>I second that notion. Narratives about revolution often involve putting the many before the few, and ideals over people (including people's lives).<br /> <br /> To build on that, though, maybe an incentive mechanic to sacrifice Ties and reinforce Principles for power of some kind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:32:37-07:00","id":896743,"title":"","content":"I don't know, if you've got a revolutionary motivated in general by love of their people (or circumstantially by hatred for their oppressors).<br /> <br /> I was thinking about the idea of narrowing the Excellency to only apply to revolutions, but then it felt too narrow to me; like the idea of a Chosen of Medicine who might have powers using the logic or style of medicine while not actually being applied to it, to have an Exalt who is able to apply revolutionary method and motivation to things other than revolution.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:51:22-07:00","id":896761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/27912-lioness-ramblings?p=896731#post896731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stories about Revolutions are full of examples of people putting their ideals before their personal relationships (often to the detriment of both)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if that should be reflected by the excellency though. Pushing the people he cares about away is partially Tyler Durden's job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T06:44:26-08:00","id":1008514,"title":"","content":"I've not forgotten this, I've had more ideas from Mr Robot and decided I'd prefer the Agent of Chaos to be more integrated with charms that interact with it rather than have its own charms.<br /> <br /> I've also come to realise how potent the charm Prince's Doom really is, in Mist the Eternal Revolutionary's hands it's basically Hail-Shattering Practice but when you factor allies it's something that lets you interfere with basically every opposed roll provided you're opposing a ruler and the greater the number of dice being thrown around the more likely it is that Prince's Doom will be able to change the outcome of a potentially pivotal roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness",